{
  "title": "Migration",
  "description": "Upgrades a document body by exactly one schema version. A migration is pure: the body is its only input. It must not read or write anything outside it (no network, loader, GPU, clock or randomness), must not mutate its input, and must return the same output for the same input. Whatever cannot be computed from the body alone belongs to the loader that builds the runtime object, not to the document. `from` and `to` must be number literals (`readonly from = 1`) for the compile-time chain checks of MigrationChain to see them.",
